-- Rollback for 20261106160010_sec_workflow_guard_helper_grants.sql
--
-- READ THIS BEFORE RUNNING IT.
--
-- This restores EXECUTE on both guard helpers to anon and authenticated, which
-- is the state migration A accidentally left behind. Running it reopens the
-- cross-organization workflow existence oracle described in the forward
-- migration: any logged-in user can probe a workflow uuid and distinguish
-- "does not exist" from "exists in another organization".
--
-- There is no functional reason to run this. Nothing calls these helpers over
-- the API. The four workflow functions that use them are SECURITY DEFINER owned
-- by postgres and reach them regardless of these grants, so restoring the
-- grants fixes nothing and only widens access.
--
-- It exists because every migration in this project is paired with its inverse,
-- and because an operator who needs to return the database to its exact
-- post-A state should be able to do so deliberately rather than by hand.

GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.assert_workflow_readable(uuid) TO anon, authenticated;
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.assert_workflow_admin(uuid) TO anon, authenticated;
